content:
Purpose:

Quick personal scratch to capture a compact format and assembly process for "tracelets" — tiny, privacy-safe call fragments we can capture at the proxy layer to allow offline deterministic replay and fast RCA without full traces. Goal is something lighter than full span/tree exports but richer than a single event.

Context / why: 
- Full traces are heavyweight and often not available (sampling, retention).
- Engineering frequently asks for reproducible short call slices when debugging model falls / latency spikes / KV cache misses.
- We want a capture that: deterministic-replays the same request path + env enough to reproduce, fits into single row in KV store, and is safe for customer PII policies.

High-level requirements (tradeoffs):
- Small: target < 4KB compressed per tracelet avg.
- Deterministic: include all inputs needed for deterministic replay of runtime decisions (route chosen, model variant, KV cache keys observed, prefix tokens, binary flags).
- Privacy-safe by default: PII redaction/masking rules before storage.
- Indexed: must include keys useful for searching (request id, tenant id, model id, error code, probe timestamp).
- Versioned: schema version in envelope to allow rolling changes.

Tracelet envelope (concept):
- id: uuid v4 (string)
- schema_version: int (start 1)
- captured_at: ISO8601
- tenant: tenant_id (hashed)
- sampling_hint: why captured (error, manually requested, heuristic)
- route_snapshot: route id + routing decisions (list of short strings)
- model_snapshot: model id + pinned version + quant profile
- request_input_summary: short tokens/metrics (#tokens, tokenized prefix hash)
- kv_cache_digest: list of cache key fingerprints observed
- outbound_calls: sequence of small records for the downstream calls taken (to model, to plugin), each: (service, path, latency_ms, status, sampled_response_digest)
- local_telemetry: latency breakdown (ingress, transform, infer, egress)
- deterministic_seed: small blob used to feed deterministic RNG on replay (e.g., sampling decisions)
- user_context_masked: free-form context but masked (see privacy rules)
- replay_artifact: optional compressed payload (minimal input + env) that the replay harness will use

Compact proto sketch (text):
message TraceletEnvelope {
  string id = 1;
  int32 schema_version = 2;
  string captured_at = 3;
  string tenant_hash = 4;
  string sampling_hint = 5;
  repeated string route_snapshot = 6;
  string model_snapshot = 7;
  RequestSummary request_input_summary = 8;
  repeated bytes kv_cache_digest = 9;
  repeated OutboundCall outbound_calls = 10;
  Telemetry local_telemetry = 11;
  bytes deterministic_seed = 12;
  bytes user_context_masked = 13;
  bytes replay_artifact = 14;
}

message RequestSummary {
  int32 token_count = 1;
  bytes prefix_token_hash = 2;
  bytes instruction_signature = 3; // compact fingerprint of the prompt ops
}

message OutboundCall {
  string service = 1;
  string endpoint = 2;
  int32 latency_ms = 3;
  int32 status = 4;
  bytes response_digest = 5;
}

message Telemetry {
  int32 ingress_ms = 1;
  int32 transform_ms = 2;
  int32 infer_ms = 3;
  int32 egress_ms = 4;
}

Compact JSON variant: when we store in KV or ship to observability, we want a base64 proto payload plus a skinny JSON index: 
{
  "id":"...",
  "tenant_hash":"...",
  "captured_at":"...",
  "model_snapshot":"...",
  "error":true,
  "size_bytes":1234,
  "payload_b64": "H4sIA..."
}

Assembly rules (proxy-side) — where we get pieces: 
- route_snapshot: from routing decision tree after route() returns — include short tags (region, tier, path)
- model_snapshot: from model catalog cache object used by the request context
- kv_cache_digest: compute MurmurHash64 of keys looked up by the request path; only include fingerprint not raw keys
- request_input_summary: compute token_count via local tokenization library and a prefix SHA256 truncated 8 bytes
- outbound_calls: instrument proxy outbound ops (non-invasive) and record lightweight metadata and response fingerprint (sha1 truncated)
- replay_artifact: created only when capture_reason in (manual, failure+repro-needed). Should be compressed (zstd) and scrubbed.

Privacy & scrubbing rules (strong by default):
- Never store raw user messages or plain-text PII in tracelet. Instead: store masked versions and fingerprints.
- Masking precedence: explicit allowlist fields (internal service ids) > hashed tokens > redacted text.
- Tenant identity stored as keyed HMAC(tenant_id) with rotating key per region.
- Replay_artifact encryption: customer-specific public key if provided, otherwise system key with short TTL access.

Sampling / retention: 
- Capture policies:
  - Error-sampled: 100% for error >= 500; 10% for 4xx;
  - Heuristic: spiky latencies, high token consumption, manual on-demand.
  - Manual capture via admin API (tracelet:force-capture)
- Retention: default 7d, extended on-demand + compliance teams. Index snowball to S3 cold storage for long-term RCA.

Replay harness (notes):
- Lightweight harness that accepts tracelet replay_artifact + deterministic_seed. It will:
  - create a sandboxed runtime with same model_snapshot and routing flags,
  - restore KV cache state from digest heuristics (not full content),
  - replay input and compare outbound_calls response_digests to recorded digests.
- Differences produce a short comparison report (diff of latency buckets, mismatch flags).

Operational metrics to emit:
- tracelet.size_bytes (histogram)
- tracelet.capture.reason (counter)
- tracelet.replay.success_rate (gauge)

Open questions / discussion items:
- How much of KV cache must we materialize to meaningfully replay cache-miss bugs? Fingerprints may not be enough. Possible solution: selective materialization on-demand (if authorized).
- Can we rely on tokenization stable across releases? We must include tokenizer version in envelope.
- How to ensure replay has deterministic plugin behavior (external webhooks)? Provide plugin stubs or recorded responses in outbound_calls.

Next actions (short):
- Prototype proto + encoder/decoder in proxy (Riley) — 2d spike.
- Add admin API to pull tracelet (Nina) and small playground UI to replay (opt-in).
- Draft privacy playbook and key rotation plan (security).

TODO checklist: 
- [ ] finalize proto fields for schema v1
- [ ] implement base64 protobuf + zstd path
- [ ] add maskers for top-10 PII patterns
- [ ] run performance microbench for capture overhead (target < 1ms p50)

Notes to self: keep the envelope intentionally minimal, prefer fingerprints over raw content. If we need more data for a particular RCA, use the admin flow to rehydrate on-demand with customer consent.

-- end of scratchpad --
